/*--------------------------------*- C++ -*----------------------------------*\
  VMFLGPU005 -- STANDARD k-OMEGA (Wilcox). FIRST-HAND from the plain
  import_files/VMFL052_natural.cas: (kw-std-on? #t), (kw-sst-on? #f),
  (rng-ke-on? #f), (realizable-epsilon? #f), (laminar? #f), and the near-wall
  regime (kw-low-re-mod? #t), (kw-wall-omega-treatment-r13? #t) -- i.e. Ansys ran
  standard k-omega with LOW-RE corrections, INTEGRATING TO THE WALL (y+ ~ 1), NOT
  wall functions. Reproduced here as OpenFOAM's standard kOmega on a boundary-
  layer-resolving mesh with CONTINUOUS (tanh) wall functions.

  DECLARED MODELLING DIFFERENCE (Ruling 4): OpenFOAM's standard kOmega does NOT
  carry Fluent's exact low-Re viscous-damping terms. kOmega is registered as OUR
  reproduction; byte-identity with Fluent's low-Re k-omega is NOT claimed.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
FoamFile { version 2.0; format ascii; class dictionary; object turbulenceProperties; }
simulationType  RAS;
RAS { RASModel kOmega; turbulence on; printCoeffs on; }
